# class Shape {}  class Circle extends Shape { constructor(draw) { super(); draw() } }  circle = new Circle(one); await circle; Promise.resolve(circle)
# The constructor of Shape allocates the instance, so it is an ordinary object and no promise, whatever its class extends. It finds no `then`, so the await gives the instance itself and runs nothing.
# Nobody constructs a species of it: the one construction of Circle is that of the program, and `draw` is `one`.
